  "raw": {
    "https://norwich.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205618": {
      "title": "Accounts Payable Specialist",
      "description": "Norwich University\nJob Posting: Accounts Payable Specialist Norwich University \n\tJob Posting: Accounts Payable Specialist Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Accounts Payable Specialist Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Financial Affairs Locations: Northfield, VT Posted: Oct 8, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: S00002 Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $19.23 - $24.04 Position ID: 205618 Share About Norwich University: Founded in 1819, Norwich University is the oldest private military college in the country and the birthplace of the Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC). Today we are a diversified academic institution that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees and professional certificates to adult learners online and to Corps and civilian lifestyle students on campus. Norwich faculty and staff challenge all of our students to push themselves academically, socially, and as leaders. Our graduates build upon their Norwich educations to launch or grow careers and make outsized contributions to their communities, the nation, and the world. Norwich University is located in the beautiful Green Mountains of Vermont, only 20 minutes from the state capital, Montpelier, and three hours from Boston or Montreal. It is a private institution nestled in a rural setting with a campus size of 1,200 acres. Our excellent benefit package includes medical, dental, vision, group life, and disability insurances, flexible-spending accounts for health and dependent care, a 403(b) retirement plan with employer match, an employee assistance program, paid time off, use of the University pool and fitness center, and tuition scholarships for eligible employees and their family members. Some employees may qualify for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program on their Federal Student Aid Direct Loan balance. For more information about our benefits, visit https://norwich.trgportal.com . Job Description: Fulfills the mission of Norwich University by being responsible for the accurate and timely processing of accounts payable transactions while supporting operational efficiency, financial controls, and vendor relationships. Administers invoice processing workflows, supports ERP and AP automation systems, ensures compliance with company policies and audit requirements, and contributes to continuous improvement initiatives within the Finance organization. Collaborates closely with vendors, procurement, and internal stakeholders to ensure effective payment management and strong financial stewardship. This is a 40 hour per week and 52 weeks per year 1.0 FTE position. Essential Functions Administers invoice processing and payment Processes vendor invoices accurately and timely. Matches invoices to purchase orders and verify supporting documentation and approvals. Codes invoices to the appropriate general ledger accounts, including prepaid expenses. Reviews and processes invoices through the OCR and workflow system. Prioritizes invoices based on payment terms and discount opportunities. Processes weekly check runs and one-off check runs as needed. Prepares cash requirements reports before check runs. Obtains required signatures on check registers and ensure timely completion. Researches missing checks, process stop payments, and reissue payments when necessary. Reconciles outstanding travel advances and ensure supporting receipts are submitted. Administers expense reimbursements Reviews and verifies travel expense vouchers and monthly reimbursement requests for faculty and staff. Reviews and approves direct pay invoices submitted by departments. Processes and assists with credit card expense reports. Supports vendor management and provides customer service. Manages vendor onboarding, maintenance, and documentation. Review sW-9 forms and validate tax information. Maintains vendor records, addresses, and tax documentation. Builds positive vendor relationships. Resolves invoice discrepancies, payment issues, overpayments, and underpayments. Responds promptly to internal and external inquiries. Maintain effective communication with departments across campus. Supports compliance, internal controls & risk management Executes and documents internal controls. Ensures compliance with segregation-of-duty requirements. Supports fraud prevention initiatives. Identifies and prevents duplicate payments and fraudulent transactions. Ensures compliance with institutional policies, audit requirements, and financial procedures. Manages unclaimed property related to outstanding checks. Maintains AP records and documentation in accordance with retention requirements. Completes reporting, analysis, and month-end activities Tracks payments to 1099 vendors and support annual tax reporting. Analyzes vendor statements and resolves discrepancies. Monitors AP aging and identify process improvement opportunities. Monitors key performance indicators including: Invoice processing cycle time Payment accuracy Discounts capture rates Invoice exception rates Supports month-end and year-end closing activities. Meets established close deadlines. Provides audit support and required documentation. Supports systems administration & process improvements Administers automated invoice processing and workflow systems. Assists with implementation and optimization of ERP and AP automation tools. Maintains and updates the Accounts Payable Manual and Check Run Procedures. Supports continuous improvement initiatives and operational efficiencies. Processes invoices within established service level expectations while maintaining high accuracy. Serves as backup to the Staff Accountant and assist with processing credit card expense reports. Monitors multiple Financial Affairs email accounts. Other Functions Maintains confidentiality of sensitive or private information. Communicates with employees, students, and others in a respectful and clear manner. Serves on University committees, councils, workgroups, or other designated bodies as assigned. Achieves, maintains proficiency in, and utilizes computers, telephones, and other job-related equipment, including related systems and software. Speaks, reads, and writes in English. Communicates by telephone, email, letter, in person, or other means or device. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor. Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent required; some college coursework with accounting courses preferred. 2 years of Accounts Payable experience preferred Proficiency with 10-key touch preferred Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Strong analytical and critical thinking skills. Ability to identify issues, research solutions, and resolve problems effectively. Excellent organizational and time management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Commitment to continuous process improvement and operational efficiency. Ability to maintain a high level of data accuracy, integrity, and confidentiality. Proficiency in MS Office (Word, Excel, SharePoint, Teams, and Outlook); (Pivot Tables, VLOOKUP/XLOOKUP, Power Query) Experience with ERP systems, experience with Banner a plus. Experience with AP automation platforms Experience with electronic payment platforms and vendor portals preferred Able to sit, squat, reach, push, pull, and manipulate related equipment; lift 15 pounds; travel outdoors to various parts of the campus. Work some evening or weekend hours. Environmental Conditions Indoor work at a computer workstation Low level of exposure to noise, dust, fumes, vibrations, and temperature changes. Additional Information: Norwich University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to providing a positive education and work environment that recognizes and respects the dignity of all students, faculty and staff. Reasonable accommodations will be made for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant.  Please contact the Office of Human Resources at nuhr@norwich.edu for assistance. All candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring immigration sponsorship, including but not limited to non-immigrant visas such as H1B, STEM, or F1, now or in the future. A post offer, pre-employment background check will be required of the successful candidate. Application Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, 3 references, and Norwich application. URL: www.norwich.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Norwich University 158 Harmon Drive Northfield, VT 05663"
    },
    "https://norwich.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205569": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Athletic Communications",
      "description": "Norwich University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Norwich University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Marketing Communications Office Locations: Northfield, VT Posted: Oct 7, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: A00296 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $41,747.00 - $45,796.00 Position ID: 205569 Share About Norwich University: Founded in 1819, Norwich University is the oldest private military college in the country and the birthplace of the Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC). Today we are a diversified academic institution that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees and professional certificates to adult learners online and to Corps and civilian lifestyle students on campus. Norwich faculty and staff challenge all of our students to push themselves academically, socially, and as leaders. Our graduates build upon their Norwich educations to launch or grow careers and make outsized contributions to their communities, the nation, and the world. Norwich University is located in the beautiful Green Mountains of Vermont, only 20 minutes from the state capital, Montpelier, and three hours from Boston or Montreal. It is a private institution nestled in a rural setting with a campus size of 1,200 acres. Our excellent benefit package includes medical, dental, vision, group life, and disability insurances, flexible-spending accounts for health and dependent care, a 403(b) retirement plan with employer match, an employee assistance program, paid time off, use of the University pool and fitness center, and tuition scholarships for eligible employees and their family members. Some employees may qualify for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program on their Federal Student Aid Direct Loan balance. For more information about our benefits, visit https://norwich.trgportal.com . Job Description: Fulfills the mission of Norwich University by assisting in advancing the visibility, reputation, and strategic storytelling of Norwich University athletics. Working within the Marketing & Communications Office (MCO), this position contributes to the development and execution of integrated communications strategies that accurately capture game day experience and statistics, highlight student-athlete achievement, enhance recruitment efforts, and elevate the Norwich brand. This role blends traditional athletic communications responsibilities with modern digital strategy, content creation, and data-informed storytelling to advance institutional priorities. This is a 40 hour per week and 52 weeks per year 1.0 FTE position. Essential Functions Assists the Director in executing programs and initiatives to deliver athletic communications objectives. Writes, edits, and distributes news releases, game recaps, feature stories, and game notes for assigned sports. Manages and executes social media strategies across platforms (Instagram, Facebook, X, YouTube, etc.), including content capture, creations, and publishing. Monitors and analyzes digital and social media performance metrics to inform strategy and improve engagement. Coordinates and manages game day communications operations, including staffing, statistics, live coverage, and media relations. Identifies, recruits, trains, and supervises student workers to support daily operations and game day responsibilities. Serves as primary media contact for assigned sports, coordinating interviews, media requests, and press coverage. Collaborates with the Marketing & Communications Office (MCO) Creative Services team on the design and production of graphics, publications, and recruiting materials. Provides digital media support, including website updates, content management, video integration, and digital asset capture and organization. Maintains and update team rosters, statistics, records, historical archives, and athletic website content. Serves as a liaison with the athletic website provider to ensure effective functionality and presentation. Proactively identifies and develops student-athlete and program stories that support recruitment and brand visibility. Ensures accuracy, consistency, and alignment with institutional brand standards across all communications and platforms. Assists with athletic events, including contests, banquets, meetings, and special events, as needed. Supports additional departmental initiatives and communications needs as assigned by the VP, AVP, or Director. Other Functions Maintains confidentiality of sensitive or private information. Communicates with employees, students, and others in a respectful and clear manner. Serves on University committees, councils, workgroups or other designated bodies as assigned. Achieves, maintains proficiency in, and utilizes computers, telephones, and other job-related equipment, including related systems and software. Speaks, reads and writes in English. Communicates by telephone, email, letter, in person, or other means or device. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required 2 years of experience in intercollegiate media relations/sports information. Experience with sports statistics (Stat Crew, Prestostats, NCAA Live Stats software) required Experience with databases, event planning, and project management preferred Proficiency in MS Office (Word, Excel, SharePoint, Teams, and Outlook) and Adobe Creative Cloud required Able to sit, squat, reach, push, pull, and manipulate related equipment; lift 15 pounds; travel outdoors to various parts of the campus Work evening, weekend, or holiday break hours Travel as needed (public or private transportation) Environmental Conditions Indoor work at a computer workstation and outdoor work at sporting events Medium level of exposure to noise, dust, fumes, vibrations, and temperature changes. Additional Information: Norwich University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to providing a positive education and work environment that recognizes and respects the dignity of all students, faculty and staff. Reasonable accommodations will be made for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant.  Please contact the Office of Human Resources at nuhr@norwich.edu for assistance. All candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring immigration sponsorship, including but not limited to non-immigrant visas such as H1B, STEM, or F1, now or in the future. A post offer, pre-employment background check will be required of the successful candidate. Application Instructions: Please provide a resume, cover letter, and Norwich application. URL: www.norwich.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Norwich University 158 Harmon Drive Northfield, VT 05663"
    },
    "https://norwich.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205525": {
      "title": "Senior Accountant - Endowment and Gifts Accounting",
      "description": "Norwich University\nJob Posting: Senior Accountant - Endowment and Gifts Accounting Norwich University \n\tJob Posting: Senior Accountant - Endowment and Gifts Accounting Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Accountant - Endowment and Gifts Accounting Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Financial Affairs Locations: Northfield, VT Posted: Oct 6, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $90,000.00 - $110,000.00 Position ID: 205525 Share About Norwich University: Founded in 1819, Norwich University is the oldest private military college in the country and the birthplace of the Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC). Today we are a diversified academic institution that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees and professional certificates to adult learners online and to Corps and civilian lifestyle students on campus. Norwich faculty and staff challenge all of our students to push themselves academically, socially, and as leaders. Our graduates build upon their Norwich educations to launch or grow careers and make outsized contributions to their communities, the nation, and the world. Norwich University is located in the beautiful Green Mountains of Vermont, only 20 minutes from the state capital, Montpelier, and three hours from Boston or Montreal. It is a private institution nestled in a rural setting with a campus size of 1,200 acres. Our excellent benefit package includes medical, dental, vision, group life, and disability insurances, flexible-spending accounts for health and dependent care, a 403(b) retirement plan with employer match, an employee assistance program, paid time off, use of the University pool and fitness center, and tuition scholarships for eligible employees and their family members. Some employees may qualify for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program on their Federal Student Aid Direct Loan balance. For more information about our benefits, visit https://norwich.trgportal.com . Job Description: Fulfills the mission of Norwich University by being responsible for the accounting, reporting, reconciliation, and compliance oversight of the University's endowment funds, donor-restricted gifts, and related investment activities. This position ensures accurate financial reporting in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP), donor intent, institutional policies, and applicable regulations. Serves as a key liaison between Finance, Development, Investment Management, and academic departments, supporting the stewardship of donor funds and the integrity of endowment accounting. The position plays a critical role in audits, annual financial reporting, and ensuring compliance with gift agreements and endowment spending policies. Hybrid work schedule may be authorized for this position. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Endowment Accounting Maintains accounting records for all endowment funds, including true endowments, term endowments, annuities, and quasi-endowments. Records endowment contributions, investment activity, spending distributions, fees, and reallocations. Reconciles endowment balances between the general ledger, investment custodian statements, and endowment management systems. Monitors compliance with donor restrictions and applicable state and federal regulations, including Uniform Prudent Management of Institutional Funds Act (UPMIFA). Calculates and records endowment spending allocations in accordance with university policies. Gift Accounting Reviews, reconciles, and monitors charitable contributions, pledges, planned gifts, and donor-restricted gifts. Ensures gifts are accurately classified and recorded in compliance with donor agreements and accounting standards. Reconciles gift activity between Development systems and the general ledger. Collaborates with Development staff to resolve discrepancies and improve data integrity. Monitors restricted fund balances and ensure expenditures comply with donor intent. Financial Reporting Prepares monthly, quarterly, and annual reports related to endowments, gifts, and restricted funds. Supports preparation of audited financial statements and related disclosures. Prepares and analyzes schedules supporting net assets with donor restrictions. Assists in developing management reports for university leadership, trustees, and investment committees. Provides financial analysis related to endowment performance, gift utilization, and fund activity. Audit and Compliance Serves as primary contact for external auditors regarding endowment, investment, and gift accounting. Prepares audit workpapers and supporting documentation. Ensures compliance with GAAP, institutional policies, investment policy, donor agreements, and regulatory requirements. Assists with implementation and documentation of internal controls over gifts, endowments, and investments. Process Improvement Identifies opportunities to enhance accounting processes, reporting capabilities, and internal controls. Participates in financial system upgrades, integrations, and process automation initiatives. Develops and maintains policies and procedures related to gift and endowment accounting. Provides training and guidance to departmental stakeholders regarding restricted funds and endowment management. Other Functions Maintains confidentiality of sensitive or private information. Communicates with employees, students, and others in a respectful and clear manner. Serves on University committees, councils, workgroups, or other designated bodies as assigned. Achieves, maintains proficiency in, and utilizes computers, telephones, and other job-related equipment, including related systems and software. Speaks, reads, and writes in English. Communicates by telephone, email, letter, in person, or other means or device. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field or equivalent work experience. 5 years of progressive accounting experience. Public accounting experience preferred. Experience in higher education or nonprofit organizations with significant endowment assets preferred. Experience with fund accounting, nonprofit accounting, higher education accounting, or endowment accounting. Strong understanding of GAAP and financial reporting principles. Knowledge of UPMIFA, donor-restricted funds, and investment accounting preferred. Experience with ERP systems preferably Banner or similar platforms preferred. Familiarity with development and fundraising systems preferred. Ability to interpret and apply donor gift agreements and fund restrictions. Excellent analytical, reconciliation, and problem-solving skills. Strong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines Ability to work collaboratively with finance, development, auditors, investment managers, and university leadership. Proficiency with financial reporting and data analysis tools. Proficiency in MS Office (Word, Excel, SharePoint, Teams, and Outlook) Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel. Work some evening or weekend hours Environmental Conditions Indoor work at a computer workstation. Low level of exposure to noise, dust, fumes, vibrations, and temperature changes. Additional Information: Norwich University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to providing a positive education and work environment that recognizes and respects the dignity of all students, faculty and staff. Reasonable accommodations will be made for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant.  Please contact the Office of Human Resources at nuhr@norwich.edu for assistance. All candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring immigration sponsorship, including but not limited to non-immigrant visas such as H1B, STEM, or F1, now or in the future. A post offer, pre-employment background check will be required of the successful candidate. Application Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, 3 references, and Norwich application. URL: www.norwich.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Norwich University 158 Harmon Drive Northfield, VT 05663"
    },
    "https://norwich.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205441": {
      "title": "Heating Plant Operator",
      "description": "Norwich University\nJob Posting: Heating Plant Operator Norwich University \n\tJob Posting: Heating Plant Operator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Heating Plant Operator Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Operations Locations: Northfield, VT Posted: Oct 2, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: M00075 Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $18.76 - $19.44 Position ID: 205441 Share About Norwich University: Founded in 1819, Norwich University is the oldest private military college in the country and the birthplace of the Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC). Today we are a diversified academic institution that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees and professional certificates to adult learners online and to Corps and civilian lifestyle students on campus. Norwich faculty and staff challenge all of our students to push themselves academically, socially, and as leaders. Our graduates build upon their Norwich educations to launch or grow careers and make outsized contributions to their communities, the nation, and the world. Norwich University is located in the beautiful Green Mountains of Vermont, only 20 minutes from the state capital, Montpelier, and three hours from Boston or Montreal. It is a private institution nestled in a rural setting with a campus size of 1,200 acres. Our excellent benefit package includes medical, dental, vision, group life, and disability insurances, flexible-spending accounts for health and dependent care, a 403(b) retirement plan with employer match, an employee assistance program, paid time off, use of the University pool and fitness center, and tuition scholarships for eligible employees and their family members. Some employees may qualify for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program on their Federal Student Aid Direct Loan balance. For more information about our benefits, visit https://norwich.trgportal.com . Job Description: Fulfills the mission of Norwich University by operating and maintaining central heating plant/ biomass systems and equipment. Essential Functions Operates boilers and auxiliary equipment for generation of 25 psi to 125 psi steam. Operates steam-driven turbines and auxiliary equipment for 480 volt, 3 phase, and power generation. Collects plant process data and logs throughout shift. Performs maintenance on equipment as required. Performs standard tests on water and steam condensate and chemically treats as needed. Follows procedures and safety rules as required. Implements lockout/tag-out and confined entry policies to comply with O.S.H.A. Performs other heating plant related responsibilities as necessary. May cross-train in other mechanical/electrical trade shops and support other Facilities Services department needs. Receives # 2 oil and wood chip deliveries at heating plant. Fills in for heating plant supervisor as needed, including taking 'on-call' pager. Reads gauges and thermometers and climb ladders. Shovels snow during winter season. Other Functions Maintains confidentiality of sensitive or private information. Communicates with employees, students, and others in a respectful and clear manner. Serves on University committees, councils, workgroups, or other designated bodies as assigned. Achieves, maintains proficiency in, and utilizes computers, telephones, and other job-related equipment, including related systems and software. Speaks, reads, and writes in English. Communicates by telephone, email, letter, in person, or other means or device. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor. Requirements: Working experience in boiler operation for 25 to 125 psi steam and turbine generator operation is preferred. Driver's license required Must know spill prevention, control, and countermeasure process for heating plant. Must have thorough understanding of combustion control systems. Must pass a post-offer, pre-employment background check and physical exam Proficiency in MS Office (Word, Excel, SharePoint, Teams, and Outlook) preferred Able to sit, squat, reach, push, pull, and manipulate related equipment; lift 80 pounds; travel outdoors to various parts of the campus Work evening or weekend hours Environmental Conditions Indoor work in a heating plant High level of exposure to noise, dust, fumes, vibrations, and temperature changes. Additional Information: Norwich University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to providing a positive education and work environment that recognizes and respects the dignity of all students, faculty and staff. Reasonable accommodations will be made for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant.  Please contact the Office of Human Resources at nuhr@norwich.edu for assistance. All candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring immigration sponsorship, including but not limited to non-immigrant visas such as H1B, STEM, or F1, now or in the future. A post offer, pre-employment background check will be required of the successful candidate. Application Instructions: Please provide a resume and Norwich application. URL: www.norwich.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Norwich University 158 Harmon Drive Northfield, VT 05663"
    },
    "https://norwich.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205364": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Norwich University\nJob Posting: Public Safety Officer Norwich University \n\tJob Posting: Public Safety Officer Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Public Safety Officer Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Public Safety Locations: Northfield, VT Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: M00058 Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $21.63 - $21.63 Position ID: 205364 Share About Norwich University: Founded in 1819, Norwich University is the oldest private military college in the country and the birthplace of the Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC). Today we are a diversified academic institution that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees and professional certificates to adult learners online and to Corps and civilian lifestyle students on campus. Norwich faculty and staff challenge all of our students to push themselves academically, socially, and as leaders. Our graduates build upon their Norwich educations to launch or grow careers and make outsized contributions to their communities, the nation, and the world. Norwich University is located in the beautiful Green Mountains of Vermont, only 20 minutes from the state capital, Montpelier, and three hours from Boston or Montreal. It is a private institution nestled in a rural setting with a campus size of 1,200 acres. Our excellent benefit package includes medical, dental, vision, group life, and disability insurances, flexible-spending accounts for health and dependent care, a 403(b) retirement plan with employer match, an employee assistance program, paid time off, use of the University pool and fitness center, and tuition scholarships for eligible employees and their family members. Some employees may qualify for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program on their Federal Student Aid Direct Loan balance. For more information about our benefits, visit https://norwich.trgportal.com . Job Description: Fulfills the mission of Norwich University by ensuring the safety and security of university students, employees and visitors on the University Campus. Utilizing a community-based policing model to support our university's vision, mission and guiding values the Officer patrols campus on foot and by vehicle to maintain good order and discipline on the campus while serving as an important community resource. This position is 52 weeks/year, 40 hours/ week. Shifts are either 10pm to 8am Sunday through Wednesday or 10pm to 8am Wednesday through Saturday. $500 signing bonus payable after successful completion of six (6) months of employment. Essential Functions Ensures the safety and protection of students, employees, and visitors and their personal property, while maintaining good order and discipline. Builds partnerships and maintains a friendly and respectful relationship with students, faculty, and staff to help resolve problems and issues that arise on campus. Works with the faculty, administration, and the student body to maintain a campus-wide perspective in matters pertaining to security and safety. Transports students as needed for a safety, illness, or injury. Provides emergency transportation service for the University, as directed by proper authority. Investigates noise and disturbance complaints, reports of theft, accidents, assaults, or other crimes as directed by the Chief of Public Safety. Respond to all campus fire or emergency calls. Consistently enforces Norwich University Rules and Regulations, including parking regulations, and reports criminal violations to the Northfield Police in accordance with Norwich University policy. Operates the Emergency notification system for the university. Notifies the proper University officials, in the event of a major incident, i.e., fire, serious water leaks, serious injury, death, or any other catastrophe. Provides and maintains a constant foot and vehicle patrol during a tour of duty. Keeps an up-to-date and accurate log of all patrol activities and incidents that occur during a tour of duty. Generates Incident Reports for all crimes, injuries, major incidents or as directed by the Chief of Public Safety. Records by receipt and in the duty log, any money or valuables turned into the Public Safety Office, maintains positive control over all accepted items, and releases them to the proper owner or custodian as soon as possible. Locks/unlocks University buildings as per the buildings schedule or as needed and turns off lights in unmanned buildings whenever possible. Notes all campus deficiencies in the log, i.e., burned out light bulbs and reports to university maintenance scheduler. When needed, answers incoming Public Safety telephone lines. Acts as the 24 hour a day, 7 days a week information hub for the University. Keeps informed on university current events in order to pass along accurate information to outside callers. Assists students and University personnel in locating persons in an emergency situation. Performs office administrative duties as assigned. Follows all safety policies and procedures. Completes all required training as determined by the Chief of Public Safety, including Campus Safety Authority (CSA) training required by the US Department of Education. Other Functions Maintains confidentiality of sensitive or private information. Communicates with employees, students, and others in a respectful and clear manner. Serves on University committees, councils, workgroups, or other designated bodies as assigned. Achieves, maintains proficiency in, and utilizes computers, telephones, and other job-related equipment, including related systems and software. Speaks, reads, and writes in English. Communicates by telephone, email, letter, in person, or other means or device. Performs other tasks as assigned by supervisor. Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent required; college courses in criminal justice or law enforcement preferred. 2 years of security, public safety, law enforcement, mental health, or social work experience preferred. CPR certified or the ability to gain certification. Valid driver's license throughout period of employment and no record of traffic violations. Must pass a post-offer, pre-employment physical exam Knowledge of the Jeanne Clery Act and/or FERPA preferred. Proficiency in MS Office (Word, Excel, SharePoint, Teams, and Outlook) Able to sit, squat, reach, push, pull, and manipulate related equipment; lift 50 pounds; push or pull up to 150 pounds; travel outdoors on foot to various parts of the campus; walk one mile within 20 minutes; climb stairs carrying prescribed equipment; pass a pre-employment physical. Able to work independently with little or no supervision. Works evening, overnight, weekend and holiday hours. Environmental Conditions Indoor work at a computer workstation and outdoors in all weather conditions. Medium to high level of exposure to noise, dust, fumes, vibrations, and temperature changes. Additional Information: Norwich University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to providing a positive education and work environment that recognizes and respects the dignity of all students, faculty and staff. Reasonable accommodations will be made for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant.  Please contact the Office of Human Resources at nuhr@norwich.edu for assistance. All candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring immigration sponsorship, including but not limited to non-immigrant visas such as H1B, STEM, or F1, now or in the future. A post offer, pre-employment background check will be required of the successful candidate. Application Instructions: Please provide a resume, 3 references, and Norwich application. URL: www.norwich.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Norwich University 158 Harmon Drive Northfield, VT 05663"
    },
