    "https://norwich.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198016": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Nursing Course Content Expert",
      "description": "Norwich University\nJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Nursing Course Content Expert Norwich University \n\tJob Posting: Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Nursing Course Content Expert Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Nursing Course Content Expert Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Nursing Locations: All Locations, United States; Northfield, VT Posted: Mar 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Contract Ref. No.: C00258 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $500.00 - $3,000.00 Position ID: 198016 Share About Norwich University: Founded in 1819, Norwich University is the oldest private military college in the country and the birthplace of the Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC). Today we are a diversified academic institution that offers undergraduate and graduate degrees and professional certificates to adult learners online and to Corps and civilian lifestyle students on campus. Norwich faculty and staff challenge all of our students to push themselves academically, socially, and as leaders. Our graduates build upon their Norwich educations to launch or grow careers and make outsized contributions to their communities, the nation, and the world. Norwich University is located in the beautiful Green Mountains of Vermont, only 20 minutes from the state capital, Montpelier, and three hours from Boston or Montreal. It is a private institution nestled in a rural setting with a campus size of 1,200 acres. Job Description: The Adjunct Graduate Nursing Course Content Expert serves as the disciplinary and academic content authority for the development or revision of an assigned graduate nursing course. This adjunct appointment is course-specific and focuses on ensuring that course content reflects current evidence-based practice, graduate-level rigor, and alignment with AACN Essentials, specialty competencies, and accreditation standards. The Content Expert collaborates with program leadership, course faculty, and instructional design staff to support effective course development and delivery. Responsibility for academic content, learning objectives, and disciplinary alignment remains faculty-led and grounded in formal nursing and educational preparation. Appointments are made on a per-course Adjunct basis, depending on program development needs. Essential Functions Course Content Development Develop or revise course content for an assigned graduate nursing course. Ensure integration of evidence-based practice, clinical reasoning, leadership, and population health concepts appropriate to graduate nursing education. Align course assignments and assessments with course objectives and program outcomes. Curriculum Alignment and Quality Participate in course review and revision processes as assigned. Maintain consistency with program curriculum framework and sequencing. Collaboration Collaborate with instructional design personnel to support course organization, accessibility, and delivery within the LMS while maintaining academic oversight of content. Work with program faculty and leadership to ensure clinical and professional relevance. Participate in scheduled development meetings as needed during the course design period. Evaluation and Continuous Improvement Support ongoing quality improvement efforts related to the assigned course. Appointment Terms Adjunct appointment for development or revision of a single graduate nursing course. Duration and compensation determined by scope of work. Position may be remote and project-based. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications MSN closely related field required. Graduate-level teaching experience in nursing education. Demonstrated expertise in the clinical specialty area relevant to the assigned course. Experience with curriculum or course development in higher education. Knowledge of AACN Essentials and graduate nursing competencies. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in Nursing (DNP or PhD) or closely related field National certification in specialty area. Experience developing online or hybrid graduate nursing courses. Prior experience with CCNE-accredited programs. Experience with competency-based or outcomes-focused education. Additional Information: Norwich University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to providing a positive education and work environment that recognizes and respects the dignity of all students, faculty and staff. Reasonable accommodations will be made for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant.  Please contact the Office of Human Resources at nuhr@norwich.edu for assistance. All candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring immigration sponsorship, including but not limited to non-immigrant visas such as H1B, STEM, or F1, now or in the future. A post offer, pre-employment background check will be required of the successful candidate. Application Instructions: Please provide a cover letter, resume, a sample of previous course development materials, and Norwich application. URL: www.norwich.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Norwich University 158 Harmon Drive Northfield, VT 05663"
